cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Si feu servir aquest programari o aquestes dades, citeu-los així.
  If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below.
title: "Genesis: abiogènesi digital (digital abiogenesis)"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: xavig-icv
abstract: >-
  A digital abiogenesis project. Programs in a random primordial soup (the BFF language of Agüera y Arcas et
  al., 2024) interact and mutate, and heritable self-replicators sometimes emerge with no designed ancestor. The project
  designs the laws of the world (space, currents, flow), never the organisms, and tests which conditions let
  life appear, become established and last, with preregistered series. The code is developed by Claude
  (Anthropic) under the direction of the project owner, and reviewed by two AI auditors; it has not been peer
  reviewed by humans. Until 30 October 2026 it was called claude-origins.
keywords:
  - digital abiogenesis
  - artificial life
  - self-replication
  - BFF
  - preregistration
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Computational Life: How Well-formed, Self-replicating Programs Emerge from Simple Interaction"
    authors:
